       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nBefore I enter it, can you tell me which of these you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum labeled dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** This would be intentional off-label dosing. If you confirm, I'll enter it with a note saying the dose is above the usual maximum.\n3. **A different regimen.** If 10 mg isn't controlling blood pressure, adding another class such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is the usual next step.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
